Cmn1=This module is used to control the \\USB-EXT-DM USB extender.  It||1
Cmn2=enables \\programmatic pairing of devices for a \\flexible USB routing||1
Cmn3=solution.\\\\Each USB-EXT-DM has a unique ID printed on\\the top||1
Cmn4=of the device.  This is used to \\associate the local and remote||1
Cmn5=ends.  If \\the ID is missing, the last six digits of \\the MAC||1
Cmn6=address can be used.\\\\Cue definition:\\The module has the following||1
Cmn7=cues:\\\\1. Module_Ready:  This signal is low while\\the module||1
Cmn8=is initializing.  Any requests \\to pair or unpair will be ignored||1
Cmn9=during \\initialization.\\\\2. Pair_Devices:  Used to associate||1
Cmn10=a \\local and remote USB-EXT-DM.\\\\3. Remove_Pairing:  Remove a||1
Cmn11=pairing from\\a device.  Used to break routes.\\\\4. Device_0/1:
Cmn12=||1These two serial joins are \\used to set the device ID on which||1
Cmn13=the \\commands are to be performed.\\\\Note: This field is a hexidecimal||1
Cmn14=field \\that must be exactly six characters long.\\Any deviation||1
Cmn15=will generate a non-fatal \\error.\\\\5. Error: Reports any errors||1
Cmn16=in the module.\\Possible Errors:\\    1: Wrong length string received||1
Cmn17=(must \\       be 6 character exactly).\\    2: Invalid character||1
Cmn18=received.  Only\\       0-9, a-f and A-F are allowed.\\    3: Failed||1
Cmn19=to create UDP socket.  \\       Module will automatically retry||1
Cmn20=if \\       this error occurs.\\\\Module Usage:\\To Pair Devices:
Cmn21=\\1. Set "Device_0" to the first device to\\be paired.\\\\2. Set||1
Cmn22="Device_1" to the second device.\\\\3. Assert the "Pair_Devices"||1
Cmn23=join.\\\\The module will automatically remove any \\pairing and||1
Cmn24=then pair the two devices.\\Note: The order of the devices is not||1
Cmn25=\\important, however only one local \\and one remote may be specified.
Cmn26=\\\\\\To Remove a Pairing:\\1. Set "Device_0" to the device that||1
Cmn27=you \\would like to unpair.\\\\2. Assert "Removing Pairing".\\\\
Cmn28=The module will remove the pairing from \\that device.\\\\Note:||1
Cmn29=Device_1 is not used with this \\command.\\\\\\If for any reason||1
Cmn30=the devices stop \\responding to the pairing commands, issue\\the||1
Cmn31="Remove_Pairing" command to all \\devices in the system and restart||1
Cmn32=the \\process.
]
